    "text": "# Investigation note: metric M331979, reporting month 2026-10-31\n\n**1. Executive finding**\nM331979 is **Amber (watch)**. Its provisional rate is **55.6% (5 of 9)**. Both the rate and the band are provisional and not confirmed by the client. Since 2026-09-30 the rate has gone down by 6.9 percentage points. But the number of non-compliant rows went up from 3 to 4. In October all 4 non-compliant rows belong to applications that were not non-compliant in September.\n\n**2. Current status and period (2026-10-31)**\n- 13 metric rows, one per application, so 13 applications.\n- 5 Compliant, 4 Non_Compliant, 3 Pending, 1 Not_Applicable.\n- Denominator is 9 and numerator is 5. The 3 Pending rows and the Exempt row are left out of the denominator. This fits the inferred denominator scope, which excludes Pending rows.\n\n**3. Movement against 2026-09-30** (provisional; each application's row compared with its row the month before)\n- **Rate:** 62.5% (5 of 8) in September, 55.6% (5 of 9) in October. Change: −6.9 pp.\n- **Who reported:** 10 applications appear in both months. 3 appear only in October and 4 only in September. Part of the change comes from this shift in who reported. It does not show that anything about the controls changed.\n- **Newly non-compliant (4):**\n  - EON679696 and EON750225 went from Compliant to Non_Compliant (reason Test_Failed). In September both already had a Fail test result but were marked Compliant under Compensating_Control_Accepted.\n  - EON735397 and EON764291 went from Pending to Non_Compliant. The reasons are No_Test_Performed and Test_Overdue.\n- **Left Non_Compliant:** EON623209 moved to Pending (Remediation_In_Progress), which takes it out of the denominator. EON848166 and EON867370 did not report in October.\n\n**4. Main contributors (2026-10-31, non-compliant rows)**\n- Super_Division_04 (Division_04_02, Division_04_04): 2 rows, legal entities Legal_Entity_21 and Legal_Entity_32.\n- Super_Division_02 (Division_02_01): 1 row, Legal_Entity_40.\n- Super_Division_08 (Division_08_02): 1 row, Legal_Entity_22.\n- No other super division and no legal entity has more than one non-compliant row. All names are synthetic.\n\n**5. Testing and exceptions (2026-10-31)**\n- 7 rows have a completed test: 5 Pass and 2 Fail.\n- 3 rows have no test (2 are Pending, Awaiting_Test_Assignment).\n- 1 test is pending and overdue.\n- 1 row is Exempt (EON634974, Exemption_Approved). It is also Exempt in September.\n- The row-level findings values on the 4 non-compliant rows are 3, 1, 5 and 4. These are provisional and should not be added up as application findings.\n\n**6. Areas for further investigation** (these are hypotheses, not confirmed causes)\n- Did the compensating controls on EON679696 and EON750225 lapse, get withdrawn, or get reclassified?\n- Do the three Pending rows waiting for testing (EON626167, EON811213, EON623209) explain how much the denominator moves from month to month?\n- The rate jumps around a lot over 12 months, from 0.0% in 2026-01 to 62.5% in 2026-02 and 2026-09. With denominators of only 6 to 9, check how much of this is noise.\n\n**7. Limitations**\n- **The band's direction may not fit this data.** The band you supplied treats a higher rate as worse. In this metric's data, though, every numerator row is a Compliant row. Please confirm which direction is correct before relying on the Amber reading.\n- The business meaning of the numerator and denominator, the metric's name and family, and its owners are not available in the data.\n- The denominators are very small, so one application can move the rate by more than 10 pp.\n- Only applications present in October are classified for movement.\n- Nothing here shows that any remediation has been completed.",
